<title>RUSSIA: LUKoil says private placement priced at 225 bp.</title>
<headline>LUKoil says private placement priced at 225 bp.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's biggest oil company NK LUKoil said on Thursday its debut international bond issue was priced to yield 225 basis points over U.S. Treasuries.</p>
<p>LUKoil said in a statement the private placement, which raised $125 million for the company, was led by CS First Boston.</p>
<p>The deal, which took place on Tuesday, was issued via LUKoil's Dutch subsidiary and had a one-year maturity.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
